From a5fdf82c2acb942eaef777f07fb017b057d780fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:20:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: macaudio: run the J716 speakers in the J616s
 frame

On the J716 every amplifier latched "bad TDM clock" about every 3 ms for
the whole of every speaker stream: 635-641 fault interrupts per 2 s
tone on the shared line, all handled (none spurious), all six amps,
with or without speakersafetyd, and none with no stream. The faults
start with the amps' unmute and end with the stream: the clock they
see is wrong for what they were set up to expect, all the time.

The J716s ADT gives the speaker serializer as
/arm-io/iop-audio-controller/audio-speaker reg = 0102 0000 0c10 0100
001bb700 fa00 0100 3000 0100 3f000000 ff0f0000 060c1810 00002010: a
12 MHz bit clock (0xb71b00) in a 250-bit frame (0xfa) at 48 kHz, six
32-bit playback slots (mask 0x3f) and twelve 16-bit sense slots (mask
0xfff). That is the J616s and J713 speaker link, which macaudio runs as
I2S with an inverted frame clock and a normal bit clock in a 250-bit
secondary frame. The J716 entry took macaudio's defaults instead
(inverted bit clock, 256-bit frame, as the J714 does), so the amps
sampled the frame clock and their data on the edge the serializer
changes them on.

Give the J716 entry the J616s speaker format and the 250-bit secondary
frame. The format applies to the speaker back-end only, through a new
speaker_dai_fmt: on the J716 the jack shares the card, on a different
serializer (a 64-bit frame) whose format is unverified, and keeps the
default. Other machines are unchanged.

On the J716 with this change: no clock fault in three 2 s six-channel
tones (one with speakersafetyd stopped) and a Speaker Switch toggle,
11-20 interrupts per tone on the shared line (the muted amplifiers'
expected clock latches at the stream end), against about 638 before;
the amplifiers read TDM_CFG1 0x02 and TDM_CFG4 0x13.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index e73aeb7864ca..b1701a5364c6 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -121,6 +121,12 @@ struct macaudio_platform_cfg {
 	unsigned int dai_fmt;
 	unsigned int primary_bclk_ratio;
 	unsigned int secondary_bclk_ratio;
+	/*
+	 * The speaker back-end's DAI format when it differs from the card's
+	 * (dai_fmt): a card whose jack and speaker serializers the firmware
+	 * runs with different bit clock edges.
+	 */
+	unsigned int speaker_dai_fmt;
 	/*
 	 * The front-ends' CPU component is their PCM provider as well: no
 	 * platform lookup by OF node, which takes every component on that
@@ -1236,6 +1242,8 @@ static int macaudio_parse_of(struct macaudio_snd_data *ma)
 							    ncodecs_per_cpu, cpu, codec);
 			if (ret)
 				goto err_free;
+			if (speakers && ma->cfg->speaker_dai_fmt)
+				link->dai_fmt = ma->cfg->speaker_dai_fmt;
 
 			link_props->is_speakers = speakers;
 			link_props->is_headphones = !speakers;
@@ -2481,6 +2489,15 @@ struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j713_cfg = {
  * dai-link 0 (cout/cin, a 2 x 32-bit frame), speakers on dai-link 1 (base-ns
  * TX0, V/I sense back on RX0).
  *
+ * The J716s ADT describes the speaker serializer as the J616s's
+ * (/arm-io/iop-audio-controller/audio-speaker reg: a 12 MHz bit clock in a
+ * 250-bit frame at 48 kHz, six 32-bit playback and twelve 16-bit sense
+ * slots), so the amps take the J616s link: I2S with an inverted frame clock
+ * and a normal bit clock, and a 250-bit secondary frame. With macaudio's
+ * default (inverted bit clock) all six amps latched "bad TDM clock" all
+ * through every stream. The jack keeps the default format: its serializer
+ * is a different one (64-bit frame) and has not been tested.
+ *
  * Bring-up values until a speakersafetyd profile is measured on AID41:
  * -30 dB with or without the daemon holding the volume (safe_vol and
  * max_vol), as the J714 ran before its profile was trusted. Each amp's
@@ -2495,7 +2512,10 @@ struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j716_cfg = {
 	.safe_vol = -30,
 	.max_vol = -30,
 	.fe_dai_names = { "j714-pcm-0", "j714-pcm-1", "j714-pcm-2" },
+	.speaker_dai_fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC |
+			   SND_SOC_DAIFMT_GATED | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_IF,
 	.primary_bclk_ratio = 64,
+	.secondary_bclk_ratio = 250,
 };
 
